<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">5 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 5 August, from 642 to 1962.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/642">642 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,384 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Penda of Mercia defeats and kills Oswald of Northumbria at Maserfield</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia">Penda of Mercia</a>, allied with the Welsh kingdom of Gwynedd, defeated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswald-of-northumbria">Oswald of Northumbria</a>, probably at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswestry">Oswestry</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shropshire">Shropshire</a>. Oswald was killed and later venerated as a saint, and the victory made Penda the most powerful ruler in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-maserfield">Battle of Maserfield</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1100">1100 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">926 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry I is crowned King of England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Three days after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-ii-of-england">William Rufus</a> died in a hunting accident, his brother Henry was crowned at Westminster. His Charter of Liberties and administrative reforms made him one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>'s ablest medieval kings.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1305">1305 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">721 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Wallace is handed over to the English at Robroyston</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Sir John de Menteith, a Scottish knight loyal to Edward I, turned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-wallace">William Wallace</a> over to English soldiers at Robroyston, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glasgow">Glasgow</a>. Wallace, who had won at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stirling">Stirling</a> Bridge in 1297, was taken to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> and executed for treason.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-wallace">William Wallace</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-war-of-scottish-independence">First War of Scottish Independence</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1583">1583 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">443 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sir Humphrey Gilbert claims Newfoundland for England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At St John's harbour, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humphrey-gilbert">Humphrey Gilbert</a> claimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a>, an early step in English overseas expansion. No settlement followed, and Gilbert was lost at sea on the voyage home.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humphrey-gilbert">Humphrey Gilbert</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1858">1858 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">168 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The first transatlantic telegraph cable is completed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Cable ships landed the ends of the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telegraph">telegraph</a> line across the Atlantic in Ireland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a>. It carried messages for just three weeks before failing, but proved the idea possible.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1884">1884 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">142 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cornerstone laid for the Statue of Liberty's pedestal</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The cornerstone of the pedestal was laid on Bedloe's Island in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Harbor. Americans had to raise the funds for the base, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> paid for the statue itself.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1914">1914 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">112 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An electric traffic signal is installed in Cleveland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An electric traffic signal with red and green lights was installed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euclid">Euclid</a> Avenue and East 105th Street in Cleveland, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohio">Ohio</a>. It is often cited as the first of its kind in the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euclid">Euclid</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1962">1962 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">64 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marilyn Monroe is found dead in Los Angeles</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Marilyn Monroe was found dead at her home in Brentwood, aged 36; the coroner ruled probable suicide from barbiturates. Her death cut short the career of Hollywood's most famous star.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 5 August <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ladislaus-iv-of-hungary"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ladislaus-iv-of-hungary.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ladislaus IV of Hungary</span><span class="tp">1262–1290</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alexander-jagiellon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alexander-jagiellon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alexander Jagiellon</span><span class="tp">1461–1506</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/vitus-bering"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/vitus-bering.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Vitus Bering</span><span class="tp">1681–1741</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
